condition_name: Hepatitis
condition_slug: hepatitis
source: NSTG 2022
introduction: "Diffuse inflammation of the liver that can be caused by infective agents, drugs, alcohol, autoimmune and toxins"
clinical_features[2]:
  - type: Acute hepatitis
    features[4]: Mild-to-moderate jaundice,Vague right upper quadrant discomfort,Fever With or without mild fever,Hepatomegaly.
  - type: Chronic hepatitis
    features[2]: General malaise/Fatigue,Re-occurence of jaundice.
investigations[6]: Liver Function Tests,"Serologic markers of Hepatitis A, B, C, D and E",Viral load,Abdominal ultrasonography,Prothrombin time,HIV Screening
treatment:
  goals[2]: Provide supportive measures,Prevent progression to chronic phase
  non_drug[3]: High carbohydrate and Normal protein diet,Discontinuation of hepatotoxic medication,Bed rest
  drug[8]: "Pegylated interferon alfa -2b: 180μg sc. weekly for 48 weeks for Chronic Hepatitis B",Oral Tenofovir 300 mg daily for Chronic Hepatitis B,"Pegylated interferon alfa-2b: 180 microgram subcutaneously weekly for 48 weeks for Chronic Hepatitis C","Ribavirin: 400 mg orally twice daily for adults with body weight less than 65 kg for Chronic Hepatitis C","Ribavirin: 400 mg in the morning and 600 mg in the evening for adults weighing 65-85 kg for Chronic Hepatitis C","Ribavirin: 600 mg twice daily for adults weighing over 85 kg for Chronic Hepatitis C",Peg IFN + Ribavirin + Sofosbuvir for 12 weeks for Chronic Hepatitis C (For all genotypes),Treatment of HBV is effective for HDV.
  adverse_reactions_and_cautions[5]: Interferon alpha 2b and Ribavirin reduce haematopoiesis,Flu-like illness,Leucopenia,Psychiatric-like symptoms,Development of early resistance if therapy exceeds one year
  supportive_measures[0]:
differential_diagnoses[0]:
complications[3]: Liver failure,Bleeding tendencies.,Cirrhosis/Liver cancer
prevention[0]:
other_investigations: null
definitive_treatment: null
prognosis: null